• completion of preclinical laboratory tests, animal studies and formulation studies conducted according to Good Laboratory Practices or other
applicable regulations;
• submission to the FDA of an IND application, which must become effective before human clinical trials may begin;
• approval by an independent institutional review board, or IRB, representing each clinical site before each clinical trial may be initiated;
• performance of adequate and well-controlled human clinical trials to establish the safety and efficacy of the proposed drug for its intended use,
conducted in accordance with current Good Clinical Practices, or cGCP, which are ethical and scientific quality standards and FDA
requirements for conducting, recording and reporting clinical trials to assure that the rights, safety and well-being of trial participants are
